      "id": "yeats-collected-poems-s0406-p00851",
      "source_en": "(page 145)\nWhen I was a child at Sligo I could see above my grandfather's trees a little\ncolumn of smoke from 'the pern mill,' and was told that 'pern' was another\nname for the spool, as I was accustomed to call it, on which thread was wound.\"\n One could not see the chimney for the trees, and the smoke looked as if it came",
